!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/32/app/order-1.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  The domain types the orders service exchanges.

  A schema of its own, not part of the API description, because the two version independently: a
  second version of the API imports this same order-1.tn, and a change to the order shape is
  order-2.tn without touching either API. Keeping them separate is what UPSTREAM.md #11's fix
  bought -- before it, a schema could reference types from exactly one other, so all of this had to
  live in the API file.
  """
{
  order => { sku: non_empty_text  quantity: int32 }
}
